{"metadata":{"name":"Sahih al Bukhari","section":{"29":{"eng-name":"Virtues of Madinah","ara-name":"كتاب فضائل المدينة"}},"section_detail":{"29":{"hadithnumber_first":1867,"hadithnumber_last":1890,"arabicnumber_first":1867,"arabicnumber_last":1890}}},"hadiths":[{"hadithnumber":1873,"arabicnumber":1873,"text":"Rapporté par Abu Huraira : Si je voyais des daims paître à Médine, je ne les poursuivrais pas, car le Messager d’Allah (ﷺ) a dit : « (Médine) est un sanctuaire entre ses deux montagnes. »","grades":[{"name":"Imam Bukhari","grade":"Sahih"}],"reference":{"book":29,"hadith":7},"chapter":{"id":4,"ara-name":"باب لاَبَتَىِ الْمَدِينَةِ","eng-name":"The two mountains of Al-Madina","isFirstHadith":true}}]}